  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]/impl[GraphWithChangingEdges/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is acceptable.\n\n- **Form:** It sits on an explicit function with a body. The explanation is in fenced citation commentary, which the built-in requires.\n- **Substance:** The reason is a deliberate design choice, not difficulty. The test covers edge inspection only. Its stored records assert only `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` dependencies. `node_content` is a required `Domain` method (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/fn[node_content]`), so the test has to define it. The body is `panic!(\"edge inspection must not read node contents\")`. Executing it would mean an unwanted content read and would fail the guard.\n- **Agreement with source:** The test supplies no other contents. `GraphWithChangingEdges` implements the other `Domain` methods (`outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`) without touching content. The assertions cover only edge dependencies and the edge-tool results. The commentary matches this code.",
